# =============================================================================
# DATABASE (Supabase Postgres via Drizzle + postgres-js)
#
# Supabase gives you two connection strings — use each for a different purpose:
#
# 1. DATABASE_URL — Transaction pooler (port 6543)
#    → Used by the Next.js app at runtime (serverless-safe, prepare:false)
#    → Dashboard: Project Settings → Database → Connection pooling → Transaction
#
# 2. DIRECT_URL — Direct connection (port 5432)
#    → Used by drizzle-kit for migrations (needs a persistent connection)
#    → Dashboard: Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI
#
# Format: postgresql://postgres.[project-ref]:[password]@[host]:[port]/postgres
# =============================================================================
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[project-ref]:[password]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.[project-ref]:[password]@db.[project-ref].supabase.co:5432/postgres"

# =============================================================================
# SUPABASE
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# Using Supabase's current key naming (publishable/secret, replacing anon/service_role).
# The two client-safe values need the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix so Next.js inlines them
# into the browser bundle — that's a Next.js requirement, not a Supabase one.
# =============================================================================
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://[project-ref].supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."

# Secret key — NEVER expose this to the client. Server-side only.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY="sb_secret_..."

# Reserved for future asymmetric JWT verification (not yet used in code).
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL="https://[project-ref].supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json"

# The app also provisions a private "pledge-proofs" Storage bucket (proof-of-
# payment uploads for manual bank/Mobile Money pledges) using this same
# service-role key — no separate variable needed.

# Note: Stripe is not currently wired up. Giving is manual (bank transfer /
# Mobile Money) via /give, reviewed by an admin in /admin/pledges. Partnership
# tiers (Stripe subscriptions) were removed for now — see src/lib/tiers.ts for
# the tier constants that replaced src/lib/stripe/tiers.ts.
